            <ArticleTitle>The roles of drug therapy given via the endotracheal tube to neonates.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>F277-F281</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/archdischild-2016-311711</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Many drugs are given to intubated neonates by the inhalation route. The optimum aerosol delivery system, however, has not been identified and there are many challenges in delivering drugs effectively to the lower airways of intubated neonates. The effectiveness of surfactant in prematurely born infants and nitric oxide has been robustly investigated. Other drugs are being used on very limited evidence.</AbstractText>
